WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.067 line:92%
-The last time you were here

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.836 line:92%
was to talk about the film

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:03.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Get Out."
-Yes.

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:06.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And so since I last saw you
here, you won an Oscar.

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:08.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm-hmm.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:12.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You were a producer
on "BlacKkKlansman" this year.

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:14.147 size:84% position:42%
So you were nominated
for an Oscar this year.

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:17.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, I was Oscar adjacent.
-Oscar adjacent.

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:19.753
Did you enjoy --
did you enjoy this year as well,

00:00:19.753 --> 00:00:22.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
being at the Oscars?
-Yes, it was fun.

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:23.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean a little bit
of the load off,

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:27.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause I knew if I won
for best picture,

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:30.363
I wouldn't have to talk,
because it's clearly Spike's --

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:32.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right, Spike.
And so that must be --

00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:34.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean the year before
where you ended up,

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.935
and you did have to speak,
and you did a great job.

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:37.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
-But that must be in the back

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:38.104 line:92%
of your head the whole time.

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:39.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, you're just kind of,
like, the whole thing.

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:41.775 size:78% position:39%
You missed the thing
'cause you're like...

00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:44.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Thank my mom. Thank my mom."
It's -- yeah.

00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:48.581
It's much -- it's much easier
to just kind of watch the show.

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:51.718 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's fantastic.
And you -- I know, obviously,

00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:54.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Get Out" was a sensation,
continues to be.

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:57.524
You have an idea for a "Get Out"
you've been pitching.

00:00:57.524 --> 00:01:00.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not a "Get Out" sequel.
A "Get Out" ride.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:02.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. Ah, yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:04.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, you know, 'cause I work
with Universal Studios.

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:05.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-So I have the fast track.

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:08.334
So, I've been pitching the ride.
You've got to be --

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:11.204
-Naturally it doesn't, when you
see that film, you don't think,

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:13.239
"Oh, this is definitely going to
have an amusement park ride.

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:14.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-No, you don't.

00:01:14.174 --> 00:01:19.312
You don't presume that,
and they haven't bit yet.

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:20.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:21.147 line:92%
-You know, they're still --

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:22.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm still waiting
for their response.

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:23.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-But the pitch is, like,

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:26.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
you have to be this color
or darker to enter.

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:26.586 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay.

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:27.887 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Audience groans ]

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:29.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.389 --> 00:01:32.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
These are the jokes.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:33.626 line:92%
No, it turns out there is

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:35.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
already a "Get Out" ride
in existence.

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:37.664 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's called America.
-Oh boy.

00:01:37.664 --> 00:01:39.332 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Audience oohs ]

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:43.203 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:46.106 line:92%
-This -- I'm very excited.

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:48.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was telling one of your
stars, Winston,

00:01:48.308 --> 00:01:49.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I'm going to
the premiere tonight.

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:53.780
And I'm thrilled, because I
watched "Get Out" on a screener

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:54.781 line:92%
when you were coming last time,

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:55.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
and so I didn't get to see it
with people,

00:01:55.949 --> 00:01:58.284
which I feel like -- I mean,
it was amazing, but you want to

00:01:58.284 --> 00:01:59.853
see it with people, so I'm
so excited about tonight.

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:02.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm particularly excited,
because 20 years ago,

00:02:02.322 --> 00:02:04.457 size:84% position:42%
you and I were going to
horror movies together.

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:05.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-So this will be like

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:07.460
the first horror movie I've gone
to with you in 20 years.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:09.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you wrote and directed it.
-And I made it.

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:11.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
-When did you get the idea
for this one?

00:02:11.898 --> 00:02:16.302
-The idea came, you know --
I've been terrified of the idea

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:18.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
of doppelgangers
since I was a kid.

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:20.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had, you know --
I always had this vision

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:24.043 align:start size:94% position:6%
of like seeing myself across
the subway platform.

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:26.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
And just kind of thought,
like, what if you saw yourself

00:02:26.713 --> 00:02:29.716
and then like, if that's not
creepy enough, what if you went,

00:02:29.716 --> 00:02:31.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
like...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:34.988 size:84% position:42%
You know? The other you
sort of smiled at you.

00:02:34.988 --> 00:02:36.222 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this kind of,
this idea of like,

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:39.626
all right what's that about?
And, you know, I've been --

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:43.296 size:84% position:42%
I put it -- the idea of
a doppelganger family,

00:02:43.296 --> 00:02:44.330 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I thought was like okay.

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:46.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, then my imagination
went crazy,

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:48.168 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and out came this film.

00:02:48.168 --> 00:02:49.302 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-That's so wonderful.

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:52.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you had a cast then
who had to --

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:52.805 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:55.041 line:92%
Getting ideas is wonderful!

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:56.242 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:58.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
Trust me, I know writers
who don't have ideas.

00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:01.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not very happy about it.
-True.

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:02.715 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-You -- you had a cast

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:04.951
that obviously had to play
two versions of themselves.

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:06.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Obviously,

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:07.487 line:92%
it's a challenge for them.

00:03:07.487 --> 00:03:08.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was it a challenge for you
as a director

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:10.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
having to do both of
their characters?

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:14.060 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. That was -- I mean,
I don't recommend it.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:15.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:17.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Like you're doing a scene
with four actors

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:19.199 line:92%
playing against themselves.

00:03:19.199 --> 00:03:21.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's kind of like --
it's kind of like the movie

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:23.469 line:92%
"Big Business," but scary.

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:24.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Light laughter ]
No?

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:27.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Big Business?"
Bette Midler and --

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:29.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
Okay, well, I've forgotten.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:32.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't expect you to.
But no, it's very difficult.

00:03:32.412 --> 00:03:34.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've got to like plan it
right.

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:35.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
Lily Tomlin.
-There you go.

00:03:35.582 --> 00:03:38.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Represent!

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:39.485 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Lily Tomlin!

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:41.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
Lily Tomlin all day!
Represent!

00:03:41.988 --> 00:03:43.356 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:44.891 line:92%
Very difficult, as it turns out.

00:03:44.891 --> 00:03:48.795
And you have on the days
where our actors are the family,

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:49.963 line:92%
it's like fun and like light.

00:03:49.963 --> 00:03:52.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then when they come in
as the scary versions,

00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:53.700 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
it's like, ooh.

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
You just feel the crew
just like --

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:58.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Everyone's just, like, ass

00:03:58.071 --> 00:04:01.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
drops out from under them
when like Lupita walks onset.

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:05.745
-And Lupita, I mean just from
the poster, the first time

00:04:05.745 --> 00:04:06.779 line:92%
you saw her in the poster,

00:04:06.779 --> 00:04:10.049 align:start size:94% position:6%
the evil version of her
is something else.

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:12.118
I mean you would have to get --
-Still pretty somehow.

00:04:12.118 --> 00:04:13.453 line:92%
-Yeah, still gorgeous, yeah.

00:04:13.453 --> 00:04:16.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
You would have to give notes
to her in character.

00:04:16.189 --> 00:04:18.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Was she that kind of actor

00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:20.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
where --
-She totally went full

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:22.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
Daniel Day on this one.
-Yeah.

00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:24.130 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Which is totally creepy.
Yeah.

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:28.134 size:84% position:42%
I'd be -- she'd be in
her dressing room alone

00:04:28.134 --> 00:04:29.435 size:84% position:42% line:92%
for like hours waiting.

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:32.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you'd walk in,
and you know she has --

00:04:32.105 --> 00:04:33.306 size:84% position:42% line:92%
she's doing this voice.

00:04:33.306 --> 00:04:35.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Raspy voice ]
It's just really scary,

00:04:35.174 --> 00:04:36.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Normal voice ]
and really creepy.

00:04:36.142 --> 00:04:38.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you'd walk in, and she'd
just be like standing

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:40.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the corner, like,
looking at you.

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:41.881 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And you'd be like, oh!

00:04:41.881 --> 00:04:42.415 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:44.884
And then, of course, inevitably
you'd give her a note,

00:04:44.884 --> 00:04:47.186
and she'd have to say something
like, you know,

00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:50.757
[ Raspy voice ] "We need more
Chex Mix on craft services."

00:04:50.757 --> 00:04:51.424 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:54.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Normal voice ]
"Chex Mix. I got you."

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:57.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
But no, she --
her performance --

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:59.932 line:92%
The entire cast is brilliant.

00:04:59.932 --> 00:05:04.871
She -- you know,
has the job of playing the lead

00:05:04.871 --> 00:05:06.739 line:92%
and the main villain in this.

00:05:06.739 --> 00:05:08.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it's kind of like
she's doing like both sides

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:13.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the "Silence of the Lambs,"
like, spectacle on full.

00:05:13.746 --> 00:05:15.214 size:81% position:41% line:92%
It's amazing to watch.

